:: Bog Cult Intro
Following the trail of strange activities, you find yourself in the bog. Suspiciously, the trail cut off as the forest opened up into the bog. You begin to scan your surroundings before a throbbing pain fills your head and the world goes black.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Dream]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Dream
<<set $outside to 1>>
Your eyes blink open and you find yourself in a small wooden room, a flickering florescent light strobes the room revealing rotten walls and floorboards. Black ooze drips from the cracks and you swear you can spot eyes hiding between the crevices. Suddenly, you feel a damp touch to your skin as tentacles stretch from the dark holes in the floorboards binding you.
<br><br>
You start to panic, but a voice permeates the entire room drawing your full attention. It speaks in a language you cannot understand but the words alone seem to calm your soul. The tentacles caress your skin, oozing black fluid over your body as the voice slowly fades to silence.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Wake]]>><<pass 60>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Wake
<<npc Salem>><<person1>>
<<if $worn.upper.exposed gte 2 or $worn.lower.exposed gte 2>>
	<<upperwear 79>>
	<<lowerwear 71>>
<</if>>
You awaken once again in yet another unfamiliar room. You to get up but you seem to be tied down to a bed, wrist and ankle cuffs bind you to the posts. You seem to be in some kind of cell. Your thoughts are interupted as someone else in the room clears their throat. "Um hello please don't panic, I can explain."
<br><br>
A young <<personsimple>> steps out from the shadows nervously. <<His>> hair is long and black matching <<his>> flowing black robe. <<His>> eyes shine a faint purple and almost seem to glow in the darkness. "U-um... I'm sorry we have to meet under such circumstances. My name's Salem." <<His>> eyes dart around nervously. "The fellowship has felt your presence getting close to the truth and decided they needed to stop you before you did anything hasty." <<He>> whispers. "I swear we're not bad people. You just have to hear me out."
<br><br>
<<He>> unlocks your cuffs and helps you sit up. "We're the true religion of this town. That other group, the ones on Wolf Street, they're heretics. They forsook our way of life and banished our ancestors from the church. Sure our ceremonies can look dangerous from an outsiders perspective but we'd never harm anybody." <<He>> seems to believe what <<hes>> saying at least and seems to be more confident and comfortable speaking about the subject. "Um... If you would please follow me, I'd like to show you something."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next (0:10)|Bog Cult Salem Intro]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Intro
You follow Salem out from the cell and down a long corridor that opens into a large central room. "T-this is the main prayer chamber." The room is large and open, lit only by candles placed on the altar and lining the walls. "I-If you don't mind, I'd like to speak to you privately for a moment..." <<He>> stands awkwardly for a moment before walking away again.
<br><br>
You follow <<him>> down another corridor, past many doors, until you reach a door near the end of the hall. "T-this is it..." Salem slowly opens the door and beckons you to enter. The room is made of stone like the others, illuminated by smooth candles, but potted plants intersperce the room. Vines covered in flowers drape down the walls painting the would be drab room in a rainbow of shades.
<br><br>
"T-this is my room..." Salem whispers embarrassed. "I've never really shown it to anybody... But I have something important I want to discuss with you." <<He>> breathes out a sigh and continues. "Now that you know we exist, the elders aren't going to want you to leave here, but I have a plan. You can become an initiate in the fellowship. It should allow you to enter and leave as you like." Once again you notice that Salem seems to be more confident when <<hes>> thinking of solutions instead of worrying. "The initiation ceremony shouldn't take long. Just speak to me when you're ready."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Room
<<npc Salem>><<person1>>
<<if $salempunishment is 0 and $salemgone is 1>>
    Salem returns for the first time since the initiation. <<He>> looks exhausted. "Oh... hey you're still here. I wasn't sure if you'd immediately leave after the initiation or not." <<He>> begins to sit but winces and stands back up. Under <<his>> flowy sleeves you can make out faint burn marks. <<He>> notices you looking and hastily covers them up. "O-oh uh... I... It's because I let you out without letting anybody know... Please don't worry about it. I'll be fine." <<He>> gives a pained smile before sitting once more.
    <<set $salemgone to 0>>
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
    You're in Salem's room. The room is made of stone like the others, illuminated by smooth candles, but potted plants intersperce the room. Vines covered in flowers drape down the walls painting the would be drab room in a rainbow of shades.
    <br><br>
    <<if $salemgone is 0 and Time.daystate isnot "night">>
        Salem seems to be meditating in silence on <<his>> bed.
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Speak to Salem|Bog Cult Salem Speak]]>><</link>>
        <br>
